  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nTake [a landing page with multiple `<video>` tags](https://fantastic-lebkuchen-95fe39.netlify.app/) (some above the fold, and some below).\n\nToday, each `<video>` tag on such a page will kick off a preload request¹ as soon as it’s discovered. This is not great because each of these requests could be several megabytes in size; they’ll end up slowing each other (+ other, possibly more critical resources) down.\n\nI’d like to have an easy way to only kick off preload requests¹ for videos that are in the viewport, similarly to how `<img loading=\"lazy\">` works.\n\n_¹ — assuming you didn’t use `preload=\"none\"`_\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n- **`preload=\"none\"`.** You can add a `preload=\"none\"` attribute on below-the-fold videos to prevent them from preloading. However, 1) you don’t always know which videos are below the fold; 2) this creates new challenges: you must also set a poster image (or [the video looks blank](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/997ff7c0-d4e8-4c41-b521-2c8dd1058c68)); and nothing is preloaded at all (duh), making the first play slower.\n- **`IntersectionObserver`.** You can implement an `IntersectionObserver` that checks which videos are in the viewport, and flips their `preload` attribute from `none` to `auto` when they approach the viewport. However, 1) this requires JavaScript, which might take a long time to load; 2) it’s much more complex to implement and thus means much lower adoption.\n\n\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nBased on our experience building userland solutions for this at Framer, I’d love to target two use cases: 1) delaying _prefetch requests_ for videos that are outside of the viewport; 2) delaying _playback_ for autoplaying muted videos that are outside of the viewport (video “gifs”)\n\nI think this is reasonably solved with two new attributes:\n\n- `loading=\"lazy\"`: acts as an intersection observer solution, effectively setting `preload` to `\"none\"` when the video is outside of the viewport\n- `autoplay=\"lazy\"`: a new value for the existing `autoplay` attribute, indicating that the video must start playing only when it enters the viewport (and perhaps also pause when it leaves it? then a more appropriate name would be `autoplay=\"in-viewport\"`)\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
